---
import SocialButtons from './SocialButtons.astro';
---
<section class="section reveal" id="about-preview">
  <div class="container">
    <div class="about-panel">
      <aside class="profile-card" aria-label="Corey profile links">
        <div class="profile-image-wrap">
          <img src="/images/corey-profile.png" alt="Corey Voller" onerror="this.style.display='none'; this.nextElementSibling.style.display='grid';" />
          <span class="profile-placeholder">CV</span>
        </div>
        <h2>Corey</h2>
        <p>Statistician · PhD researcher · software developer</p>
        <SocialButtons compact />
      </aside>

      <div class="about-copy">
        <span class="tag">About</span>
        <h2 class="section-title">about<span class="brace">&#123;</span>Corey<span class="brace">&#125;</span></h2>
        <blockquote class="sidekick">
          Statistics, programming and visual explanation for medical research and trial methodology.
        </blockquote>
        <p>
          I enjoy exploring statistical ideas beyond routine analysis work, especially where methods can be made clearer through
          simulation, interactive graphics, reproducible notebooks or small pieces of software.
        </p>
        <p>
          My research focuses on Bayesian adaptive clinical trial designs, with broader interests in biostatistics,
          external data, evidence synthesis, R programming and practical teaching resources.
        </p>

        <table class="about-meta" aria-label="About Corey details">
          <tbody>
            <tr><td>.focus</td><td>Bayesian adaptive clinical trials, small population designs, medical statistics and simulation.</td></tr>
            <tr><td>.tooling</td><td>R, Quarto, Git, HTML/CSS, Python, C#, dashboards and reproducible reports.</td></tr>
            <tr><td>.research</td><td>Efficient design and analysis of small population clinical trials with external data.</td></tr>
            <tr><td>.teaching</td><td>Mathematics, statistics, R workflows and visual explanations of complex methods.</td></tr>
            <tr><td>.approach</td><td>Turn complicated statistical ideas into something people can inspect, question and use.</td></tr>
          </tbody>
        </table>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
